" marimo vimrc: basic Neovim keymaps ported to marimo's vim mode.
" Enable in marimo.toml (absolute path; marimo does not expand ~):
"   [keymap]
"   vimrc = "/home/<you>/.config/marimo/vimrc"
"
" marimo 0.25.2 vimrc parser rules (verified in its frontend bundle):
" - Only map/nmap/vmap/imap, noremap/nnoremap/vnoremap/inoremap,
"   unmap/nunmap/vunmap/iunmap, mapclear/nmapclear/vmapclear/imapclear.
"   No let, set, xmap, omap, <silent> or <expr>.
" - A comment is a whole line starting with a double quote in column 0.
"   Keep comments on their own line. No indented lines, no spaces in lhs/rhs.
" - No <Leader>. Your leader is Space (nvim/.config/nvim/lua/core/vimsane.lua:6-7),
"   but every leader mapping you have is a picker, buffer or LSP action, so none
"   is ported. To add one, write <Space> literally and first free it from its
"   default (Space = l):
"     unmap <Space>
"     nnoremap <Space>d dd

" Yank to the system clipboard, approximating clipboard=unnamedplus.
" Source: nvim/.config/nvim/lua/core/vimsane.lua:43
" The "+ register calls navigator.clipboard (codemirror-vim 6.4.0). Yanks also
" fill the unnamed register, so yyp and ddp still work.
" Caveats: "ay etc. now yank to "+ instead; needs a secure origin
" (localhost or https). Deletes do not go to the clipboard.
nnoremap y "+y
vnoremap y "+y

" Paste from the system clipboard. Off by default: each p asks the browser
" for clipboard-read permission, and ddp/xp would paste the clipboard
" instead of the deleted text. Uncomment to opt in.
" Source: nvim/.config/nvim/lua/core/vimsane.lua:43
"nnoremap p "+p
"nnoremap P "+P
"vnoremap p "+p

" Y yanks to end of line (Neovim built-in default, not in your config).
" Recursive nmap so it goes through the y clipboard mapping above.
" Source: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/v0.12.1/runtime/lua/vim/_core/defaults.lua#L101
" (retrieved 2026-11-02)
nmap Y y$

" Already built into marimo or codemirror-vim, so not mapped here:
